# Aelaron governance (AEGF)

Read workspace `AGENTS.md` at task start. Cross-tool mapping: `aelaron-framework-governance/docs/agents/agent-instruction-layer.md`.

## Non-negotiables

- Linked GitHub issue with `status/ready` before coding
- PRs to `development` only; human merges `main`
- Declared verification profile with CI evidence in PR
- Stay within issue envelope and allowed paths

## Cursor hooks (no stop enforcement)

- **sessionStart** — validates instruction layer and injects governance context
- **preToolUse (Task)** — injects AEGF constraints into every subagent prompt
- **afterShellExecution** — optional session mark when `governance-run-report.sh` runs

`stop` / `subagentStop` follow-ups are **disabled permanently** (they caused infinite loops).

## Governance reports (PRs and releases)

For pull requests and release promotion, run from the repo you changed:

```bash
bash .github/scripts/governance-run-report.sh \
  --run-type standard \
  --issue <NNN> \
  --profile <VP-ID> \
  --fire <comma-separated INT/EXE/VER/BRN IDs you satisfied> \
  --ci-pass <ci-context-if-passed> \
  --append-log governance/metrics/runs.jsonl
```

Include output in the PR under **Governance coverage (cumulative)** (`--for-pr`). Local agent chats do not require a pasted end-of-turn report.

Catalog: `aelaron-framework-governance/templates/governance-firing-catalog.yaml`
Roles: `aelaron-framework-governance/templates/agent-role-catalog.yaml`
